✅ Short Interview Answers

1) Modern HTTP clients in Spring?
“RestClient for sync, WebClient for reactive, HTTP Service Clients for declarative interfaces.
RestTemplate is deprecated since Spring 7.1. OpenFeign works but is in maintenance mode.”

2) Sync vs reactive vs declarative?
“Sync means the thread waits for the response.
Reactive means non-blocking I/O with Mono/Flux.
Declarative means interface-based API definition — it can be sync or reactive underneath.”

3) Can declarative also be reactive?
“Yes. HTTP Service Clients can use WebClientAdapter and return Mono/Flux.”
